    "body": "Fixes #41586\n\n## Problem\nWhen `vim.pack.add` clones a plugin repository, if the clone process is interrupted (e.g., via SIGINT), it leaves behind a corrupted plugin directory with an incomplete `.git` structure. On subsequent startups, `lock_sync()` attempts to read `HEAD` information from this interrupted clone to repair the lockfile, which raises an uncaught git error and completely crashes `vim.pack.add` execution before Neovim can start properly.\n\n## Root Cause\n1. `do_install` directly clones into the final `p.path` location. An interruption leaves that directory in place.\n2. `lock_repair` lacks error handling for its `git_cmd` / `git_get_hash` calls, causing startup to crash when it encounters the invalid repository.\n\n## Solution\n1. **Atomic Installation:** Made `do_install` clone the repository into a `.tmp` path first. It performs the clone and `checkout` there, and only uses `uv.fs_rename` to move the repository to its final destination upon complete success.\n2. **Robust Recovery:** Wrapped git commands in `lock_repair` with `pcall`. If they fail due to severe corruption (from plugins left behind by older Neovim versions), the corrupt directory is safely deleted without halting execution.\n\n## Testing\nAdded a regression test in `test/functional/plugin/pack_spec.lua` simulating a broken plugin clone. Verified that `vim.pack.add` recovers gracefully, deletes the corrupt repository, and loads other plugins successfully.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-25T10:24:02Z",
